{
  "core_message": "The crew of the Mary Celeste vanished without a trace, leaving the mystery unsolved.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "100‑foot ghost ship found empty, rum cargo untouched",
  "description": "In 1872 the Mary Celeste was found drifting in the Atlantic, perfectly seaworthy yet completely empty. Why did the crew disappear?\n\nWe explore the ship’s origins, its final voyage, and the baffling clues that still haunt investigators.\n\nKey points:\n- Built as Amazon in 1861, renamed Mary Celeste in 1868\n- Departed New York for Genoa on 7 November 1872\n- Found adrift off the Azores on 4 December 1872\n- No sign of struggle, cargo untouched\n- No evidence of foul play at the salvage hearing\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Mary Celeste\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Celeste), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.",
